  "title": "Qt: Retap when changing to or from a IO Graph LOAD graph",
  "description": "The IO Graph LOAD graphs store information in the io_graph_item_t\ndifferently to all the other advanced graphs. So if the graph\nchanges to or from a LOAD type, we need to retap.\n\nWe could instead change update_io_graph_item to instead always\ncalculate and store the LOAD related information for FT_RELATIVE_TIME\nfields, which would avoid the retapping when changing graph type,\nat the tradeoff of tapping taking longer for any field of that type.",
  "state": "merged",
